<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sistine Chapel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1473">1473</a>–<a href="/years/1481">1481</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sistine Chapel is a chapel in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apostolic-palace">Apostolic Palace</a> in Vatican City, built between 1473 and 1481 for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-sixtus-iv">Pope Sixtus IV</a>, after whom it is named. Its walls were painted by Botticelli, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/perugino">Perugino</a> and others, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michelangelo">Michelangelo</a> painted its ceiling between 1508 and 1512 for Julius II and the Last Judgement on the altar wall between 1536 and 1541. Papal conclaves are held there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sistine-chapel.jpg" alt="Sistine Chapel" width="320" height="434" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Snowdog at Italian Wikipedia. · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sistina-interno.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
